Negative control for a table always having at least one column (`R6-25`).

Lets the last visible column be taken off. The menu still works, the url is
still written, and the table it leaves behind has a header row with nothing in
it and rows with no cells — and the url cannot say "none" in a way that survives
a reload, so the set silently springs back to the full declaration on the next
visit. Only the floor is withdrawn: every other pick still behaves exactly as
before.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the column-picker spec — with one column left the remaining entry is no
longer refused, so the "the last column cannot be taken off" case fails while
every multi-column case stays green.

